  { q: 'Is this really live, or just pre-recorded videos I watch on my own?', a: 'Fully live. A faculty member teaches in real time on every scheduled session, takes questions as they come up, and adjusts pace to the batch. Sessions are recorded afterward only for your revision — nothing is pre-shot.', },
  { q: 'How does doubt-solving work if I\'m not in a physical classroom?', a: 'You can ask during the live session itself via audio, video, or chat, or raise it in our 24×7 doubt-solving channel outside class hours. Either way, a teacher — not a bot — responds.', },
  { q: 'How are online batches placed into IQ-based Series?', a: 'The same Entrance Mapping Test used for offline batches applies online. It\'s IQ-based, not knowledge-based, and places you into one of five Series so your online batchmates are at a similar ability level.', },
  { q: 'What happens if I miss a live class?', a: 'Every live session is recorded and added to your portal the same day, so you can catch up before the next weekly evaluation test without falling behind the batch\'s pace.', },
  { q: 'Do online students get the same weekly evaluation tests as offline batches?', a: 'Yes. Sectional and full-length Computer-Adaptive, Computer-Based, or Paper-Based tests run weekly for every batch, live or offline, and feed directly into course-path adjustments.', },
